WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Due to the
coronavirus outbreak,

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
many events that people look
forward to every year

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.604 size:81% position:41%
have been postponed or
called off completely.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:05.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yesterday, towns across
the country

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.907 size:78% position:39%
were forced to cancel
their Easter parades.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.142 line:92%
Well, we here at "Late Night

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:10.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
couldn't stand by
and let that happen,

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
so here is one of my writers
Amber Ruffin,

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:16.216
with the world's first
quarantine Easter parade.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.817 line:92%
-Hello. I'm Amber Ruffin,

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:21.821 size:84% position:42%
and I'm wearing a gown
because I feel like it.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.823 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Now, I love parades.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:26.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't think we shoul
all have to miss out

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the fun of Easter parades
just because

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're all locked up
in our houses.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm throwing an
Easter quarantine parade

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:37.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
for you, right now,
from my house.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.340 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh! And here comes
the first float.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:43.810 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.881
Our first float in the Easte
quarantine parade is, of course,

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.749 line:92%
the alcohols of quarantine

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, I see there's vodka,
everyone's favorite,

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:53.920 line:92%
and his best friend, tequila

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.124
Not my favorite brand, but i
was on sale, so I got two.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And triple sec.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't have a margarita
without triple sec --

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.596 size:84% position:42%
that is, until all your
triple sec runs out.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.131 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Then you can...and will!

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, those are all, of course,
evening drinks.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:12.138 line:92%
During the day, it's Moscato

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ah! And here comes
the second float

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:18.144
in the Easter quarantine parade,
jeans and bras!

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, fun fact about
these jeans --

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
I haven't worn them
for over 27 days

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don't know
if I ever will again.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:28.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
And speaking of things I'l
never wear again, bras.

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:31.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way, today's parade i
sponsored by margaritas.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:34.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
Margaritas, thank you.
I love you.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:38.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
Up next, oh,
it's the tangerines!

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
A very personal
Easter quarantine float

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
for me, because once
every two weeks,

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
my husband buys a giant ba
of tangerines.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:49.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, we have a mix of
fresh ones and old ones.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
Fun fact -- I've never seen my
husband eat a tangerine.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
He buys them, brings them home
and never throws them away

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.786 line:92%
Let's hear it for tangerines

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:02.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, we've got
a beautiful crowd out there.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:06.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, we've got
a big, shiny bulldog,

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:09.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mommy and Daddy,
and some lucky cats.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.532
Mommy and Daddy -- the onl
things keeping the peace

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
between the bulldog
and the cats.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.269 line:92%
Good job, Mommy and Daddy.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.637 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Next up, books!

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's right --
that big, fat pile of book

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
you planned on reading durin
the quarantine

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
is still there waiting
for you to crack

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.079 line:92%
at least one of them open.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:26.646 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Sorry, books.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess you'll have to wai
for the next pandemic.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:33.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
Next up, a favorite of
the Easter quarantine parade

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:36.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a dozen chocolate-chi
cookies!

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:39.993
Now, these cookies -- Wait
Where are these cookies?

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:40.660 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, that's right.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were eaten seconds afte
coming out of the oven

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:47.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
instead of dinner because we'r
more animal than human now

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
Kind of funny anyone
actually thought

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:52.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they would survive
until the next day.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, of course,
the final float in

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:57.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Easter quarantine parade
a Zoom meeting!

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:00.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's right -- your
least-favorite colleagues

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.749 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
all on one screen!

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:05.485
Now, that's it for the
quarantine Easter parade.

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:09.489
I'd like to thank everyone who
made the time to come out today,

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.424 line:92%
especially Mommy and Daddy

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:14.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd also like to thank our
sponsor, margaritas.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
Margaritas --
if it weren't for them,

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:21.367
I would have murdered my husband
by now, with a tangerine.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.569 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's it for us.

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:24.370 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Back you to, Seth.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you to Amber Ruffin
We'll be right back.

